  "text": "My App\r\n\r\nDatabase restored from a backup\r\n\r\nThe database behind My App has been REPLACED with the contents of a backup\r\narchive. The application is now serving the state it was in at 2026-03-04T05:06:07.000Z;\r\nanything written after that point is NOT PRESENT.\r\n\r\n  Restored from run:  run-3\r\n  Backup taken at:    2026-03-04T05:06:07.000Z\r\n  Restore completed:  2026-03-04T06:07:08.000Z\r\n  Triggered by:       Ada Admin\r\n\r\nA safety backup was taken immediately before the swap (run run-2).\r\n\r\nThe process that performed the restore exited immediately afterwards so a\r\nsupervisor could start one with a connection pool built against the restored\r\ndatabase. A restart at the time above is expected, not a separate incident.\r\n\r\nYou are receiving this because you can view database backups in My App.\r\nThis notification cannot be turned off, because a database being replaced\r\nshould never be silent.\r\n\r\nOpen database backup: https://app.example.test/admin/settings/db-backup\r\n\r\n--\r\nThis is an automated message from My App.\r\nIf you were not expecting it, you can safely ignore it.",
